# Files excluded from the deployment upload entirely, so they reach neither the
# build nor the serverless function bundles.
#
# This exists for the Python function. api/index.py runs with the repo root as
# its bundle root (/var/task), so anything shipped here is stored again for
# every deployment Vercel retains, and function storage is billed on that total
# rather than on traffic.
#
# The test is "does `next build` or a running function read this file", not "is
# it useful". public/ is absent from this list on purpose: the OG image routes
# read fonts and photos out of it with fs.readFileSync at build time.
#
# Every pattern is anchored with a leading slash. Without one these match at any
# depth, the way .gitignore does: a bare `supabase/` also excluded
# src/lib/supabase/, and the build failed on four unresolved @/lib/supabase
# imports.

# Backend development surfaces. Migrations run in GitHub Actions from a fresh
# checkout (.github/workflows/deploy.yml), never from the deployed function, so
# alembic/ has no reader in production.
/api/alembic/
/api/alembic.ini
/api/tests/
/api/bruno/
/api/scripts/

# Frontend tooling. npm run grain is manual and bakes to public/shelf/*.webp,
# which are committed; check-dev-ports only runs under predev:full.
/scripts/

# Local Supabase CLI config and the magic-link email template, both applied
# from a developer machine.
/supabase/

# Prose and agent config. .husky/ is deliberately NOT here: `npm install` runs
# the package.json `prepare` script, and 8 KB is not worth finding out how husky
# reacts to its own directory being gone.
/docs/
/.claude/
/.github/
/README.md
/TODO.md
